# Discriminating pair, HALF 2 of 2: a program demoted to the tree-walk
# interpreter by a WHOLE-MODULE gate, which then runs perfectly and prints a
# perfectly ordinary result.
#
# The trigger is the string literal below. `exec_core.rs`'s
# `interpreter_preference_reason` greps the entry file's SOURCE TEXT for
# `window_winit` and diverts the module before the JIT is ever attempted --
# there is no per-function split on this path, and nothing here touches
# graphics. `.claude/rules/testing.md` records the same family for `std.cli` and
# `get_cli_args`.
#
# This is the exact shape that made engine A/B claims unfalsifiable: the run
# SUCCEEDS, exits 0, and its stdout is indistinguishable from a JIT run. Only
# the receipt separates them. Its receipt must read
# `engine=interpreter demoted=yes reason=jit-unsafe-graphics ...`.
#
# Why not `d.insert(...)`, which .claude/rules/testing.md also lists: on this
# seed it does not demote, it hard-errors (`Function 'insert' not found`), so it
# cannot demonstrate the silent case. A fixture that fails loudly proves nothing
# about a defect whose entire nature is that it is quiet.
fn main():
    val backend = "window_winit"
    print "backend={backend}"
